
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
D,B,C are collinear [00]
AD ⟂ BC [01]
B,F,C are collinear [02]
BC ⟂ FE [03]
G,A,E are collinear [04]
GE = GA [05]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
H : Points
D,H,F are collinear [06]
HD = HF [07]

 * Proof steps:
001. H,D,F are collinear [06] & HD = HF [07] ⇒  H is midpoint of DF [08]
002. BC ⟂ FE [03] & AD ⟂ BC [01] ⇒  FE ∥ AD [09]
003. GE = GA [05] & HF = HD [07] ⇒  GE:GA = HF:HD [10]
004. EF ∥ AD [09] & G,A,E are collinear [04] & H,F,D are collinear [06] & GE:GA = HF:HD [10] ⇒  GH ∥ EF [11]
005. B,F,C are collinear [02] & D,B,C are collinear [00] & AD ⟂ BC [01] & EF ∥ AD [09] & GH ∥ EF [11] ⇒  GH ⟂ DF [12]
006. H is midpoint of DF [08] & GH ⟂ DF [12] ⇒  GD = GF
==========================
